{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["<b>And they chased you, as the bees do.</b> This means that they sting from this side and that, but do not kill — so too ויכם ויכתום: they pursued them with blows and wounding, but did not kill them, so that they would not open their mouths wide and the Name of Heaven be desecrated. And know this: that it does not count here the fallen in battle as in the manner of other wars. And it appears that this is the battle of the Canaanite king of Arad, for it is written there וישב ממנו שבי — but they did not kill a single one of them. And the Holy One, blessed be He, afterward took their vengeance from them, as it is said: ״וישמע ה׳ בקול ישראל ויך את הכנעני״ etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:23.114618162Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}